---
import ProseLayout from '../layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
---

<ProseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="Privacy practices for the Village of Midvale website."
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  intro="What we collect (almost nothing), how it's used, and how long we keep it."
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not use third-party analytics, advertising trackers, or
    cookies for tracking. It does not share information about your visit with
    third parties. The only personal data we collect is what you voluntarily
    submit through the contact form.
  </p>

  <h2>Server logs</h2>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider (Cloudflare) keeps short-lived logs of requests
    to the site for security, abuse prevention, and operational reasons.
    These logs may include your IP address, the page you requested, your
    browser, and the date and time. They are not joined with personal
    information and are kept for a limited period.
  </p>

  <h2>The contact form</h2>
  <p>
    When you use the contact form, the message you submit (along with the
    name, email, and any other information you provide) is delivered by
    email to the appropriate village contact and is retained as a record of
    correspondence. Public records laws (Ohio R.C. § 149.43) may apply.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your IP address may be recorded with the message for abuse-prevention
    purposes. We do not use this information for marketing, do not share it
    with third parties, and do not retain it beyond what's needed to respond
    to your request.
  </p>

  <h2>Cloudflare Turnstile</h2>
  <p>
    The contact form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to deter automated submissions.
    Turnstile is a privacy-respecting alternative to traditional CAPTCHAs &mdash;
    it does not use cookies and does not track you across sites.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly
    collect personal information from minors.
  </p>

  <h2>Updates</h2>
  <p>
    If our practices change &mdash; for example, if the village adopts an
    analytics tool &mdash; this page will be updated to reflect the change.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>
